  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 328 PM CDT Tue Aug 18 2026\n\nThe front will advance further south of the CWA by Thursday with a \nhigh pressure center arriving in its wake with dry and seasonably \ncool conditions persisting into Friday. In prevailing upper-level \nnorthwesterly flow, a shortwave trough and accompanying cold front \nwill pass sometime in the Friday evening through Saturday afternoon \ntimeframe, but the timing is uncertain. Given that moisture return \nwill be limited, only 20 to 30 percent of ensemble model membership \nhas showers and thunderstorms. Without strong/persistent low-level \nWAA, temperatures will be near to slightly below average, cooling \nfurther below average on Sunday as seasonably cool airmass and \nstrong surface high pressure center skirts the Mid-Mississippi River \nValley.\n\nEarly next week, global model guidance agrees that northwesterly \nflow will continue but vary on whether or not heights rise as a \nridge across the Rocky Mountains amplifies or heights fall as \nlongwave troughing develops across the Great Lakes. The former would \nfavor warming temperatures to above average and the latter would \nfavor a slow moderation of temperatures around average. There is not \na clear preference for either scenario in ensemble model guidance at \nthis time. Additionally, there is a signal for passing shortwave \ntroughs to provide rounds of showers and thunderstorms during that \ntime, further complicating the pattern.",
